@rolfedh So the change should be fairly straight forward, after we [fetch](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/07ed1e4e8a2adc4ee46b0108cd2d464498689842/pkg/cmd/repo/clone/clone.go#L183) the upstream repo we will want to run `git remote set-branches upstream \*`. Right now we do not have any code in the [git client](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/git/client.go) to do that so we will need to add it. 

Something like:
```go
func (c *Client) SetRemoteBranches(ctx context.Context, remote string, refspec string, mods ...CommandModifier) error {
	args := []string{"remote", "set-branches", remote, refspec}
	cmd, err := c.Command(ctx, args...)
	if err != nil {
		return err
	}
	for _, mod := range mods {
		mod(cmd)
	}
	_, err = cmd.Output()
	if err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return nil
}
```

Hopefully that is enough to get you started. Please let me know if any of that was not clear.
